{"tool_name":"desso","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"DESSO","home":"https://bmbl.bmi.osumc.edu/DESSO","summary":"DESSO is a deep learning-based framework that can be used to accurately identify both sequence and shape regulatory motifs from the human genome.","addition_date":"2019-11-14T18:30:36Z","last_update_date":"2020-12-22T06:26:42Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Database portal","Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:DESSO","credit":[{"email":"bingqiang@sdu.edu.cn","name":"Bingqiang Liu","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"qin.ma@osumc.edu","name":"Qin Ma","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence motif discovery","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0238"},{"term":"Transcription factor binding site prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0445"},{"term":"cis-regulatory element prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0441"}]}],"name":"Deep Sequence and Shape Motif (DESSO)","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/NAR/GKZ672","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019 The Author(s) 2019. Published by Oxford University Press on behalf of Nucleic Acids Research.The identification of transcription factor binding sites and cis-regulatory motifs is a frontier whereupon the rules governing protein-DNA binding are being revealed. Here, we developed a new method (DEep Sequence and Shape mOtif or DESSO) for cis-regulatory motif prediction using deep neural networks and the binomial distribution model. DESSO outperformed existing tools, including DeepBind, in predicting motifs in 690 human ENCODE ChIP-sequencing datasets. Furthermore, the deep-learning framework of DESSO expanded motif discovery beyond the state-of-the-art by allowing the identification of known and new protein-protein-DNA tethering interactions in human transcription factors (TFs). Specifically, 61 putative tethering interactions were identified among the 100 TFs expressed in the K562 cell line. In this work, the power of DESSO was further expanded by integrating the detection of DNA shape features. We found that shape information has strong predictive power for TF-DNA binding and provides new putative shape motif information for human TFs. Thus, DESSO improves in the identification and structural analysis of TF binding sites, by integrating the complexities of DNA binding into a deep-learning framework.","authors":[{"name":"Hoppe A.D."},{"name":"Li Y."},{"name":"Liu B."},{"name":"Ma A."},{"name":"Ma Q."},{"name":"Wang C."},{"name":"Wang Y."},{"name":"Yang J."},{"name":"Zhang C."}],"citationCount":8,"date":"2019-09-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"Prediction of regulatory motifs from human Chip-sequencing data using a deep learning framework"},"pmcid":"PMC6735894","pmid":"31372637"}],"topic":[{"term":"ChIP-seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3169"},{"term":"Protein sites, features and motifs","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3510"},{"term":"Transcription factors and regulatory sites","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0749"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Deep Sequence and Shape Motif (DESSO)","home":"https://bio.tools/DESSO","summary":"DESSO is a deep learning-based framework that can be used to accurately identify both sequence and shape regulatory motifs from the human genome.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:desso/cmd/bmbl.bmi.osumc.edu","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false,"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":32,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":2,"year":"2020"},{"count":2,"year":"2021"},{"count":3,"year":"2023"},{"count":3,"year":"2025"},{"count":6,"year":"2022"},{"count":15,"year":"2024"}